														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3803872">
									

<blockquote>
<p>But the Foundation needs a policy for intellectual property and patents dammit.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>And they presumably have one in-universe. But that doesn't mean we have to actually have it on the site. This is a creative writing community: pages exist to deliver a good reading experience, not to tick boxes on every facet of worldbuilding. I can understand the desire to tick those boxes, but your execution had to delivery an interesting piece of literature.</p>
<p>Beyond that, this page is also problematic due to the site's own non-fictional history with licensing issues. Adding an extra layer of fictional, in-universe licensing is <em>begging</em> for trouble.</p>

							</div>

								
					
